Mariah Carey has officially unfrozen , the clocks have gone back, and the evenings are darker, meaning the festive season is upon us.

From now on, we’ll start to see streaming platforms usher in their lineup of holiday content, and if your watchlist includes everything from festive musicals to feel-good rom-coms, keeping track of streaming subscriptions can get expensive.

DIRECTV is offering a holiday deal that could help make seasonal viewing a little more affordable. The MyEntertainment Genre Pack brings Disney+, Hulu, HBO Max and AMC+ together with more than 60 live TV channels for $34.99 per month for the first two months, down from its regular $42.99 monthly price. The offer ends Jan. 5, 2027.

Furthermore, new customers can also take advantage of a five-day free trial , making it easier to explore the lineup before signing up. Service automatically continues each month at its regular price after the trial and promo, unless canceled.

Christmas Musicals and Movies All in One Place

Paying for multiple streaming subscriptions can add up, especially during the holiday season when you&#8217;re looking to catch up on Christmas movies and musicals across different platforms. DIRECTV’s MyEntertainment Genre Pack is an attractive option this time of year, where customers can bundle several streaming platforms into one package alongside dozens of live TV channels. Rather than paying for each included streaming service separately, these subscriptions are included through a DIRECTV subscription.

For Christmas musical fans, there&#8217;s plenty to explore across the included platforms. Disney+ is home to seasonal favorites like The Muppet Christmas Carol and The Nightmare Before Christmas , while Hulu offers A Very Jonas Christmas Movie . Beyond the musicals, viewers can find holiday movie favorites, festive television specials and curated Christmas episodes of animated shows like Bob&#8217;s Burgers , The Simpsons and Family Guy .

There&#8217;s also a broad selection of kids&#8217; movies and family-friendly entertainment across Disney+ and Hulu, making the package a convenient option for households with different viewing tastes. Alongside its streaming inclusions, MyEntertainment offers more than 60 live entertainment channels, including Bravo, Comedy Central, Food Network, HGTV, History, National Geographic and many more.

