DIRECTV’s MyCinema Adds More Holiday Movie Options &nbsp;&nbsp;

For viewers who want even more classic films and seasonal programming, DIRECTV offers MyCinema as an optional Mini pack add-on to MyEntertainment. &nbsp;

The Mini pack includes 12 movie-focused channels, including Turner Classic Movies (TCM), Family Movie Classics, Hallmark Family, Hallmark Mystery, Great American Family, Grit, INSP, LMN, ShortsTV, Smithsonian Channel and Sony Movies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

TCM is a particularly appealing addition for classic film enthusiasts, with holiday favorites like Meet Me in St. Louis and The Bishop&#8217;s Wife worth looking out for when they air. Meanwhile, Hallmark&#8217;s holiday programming is practically a December tradition of its own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

MyCinema is currently available for $0 for the first two months before renewing at $10.99 per month, plus tax. Just make sure to maintain a qualifying base plan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

